  "summary": "A sewage lift station collects wastewater flowing by gravity into a wet well and pumps it up through a rising main to a higher sewer or treatment plant. Submersible non-clog pumps sit on the wet-well floor on guide rails, so they can be lifted out without entering the well. Float switches (or a level transmitter) start the duty pump at a set level, start the standby pump if the level keeps rising, stop the pumps at the low level and raise a high-level alarm. Non-return and isolation valves in a separate valve chamber allow each pump to be serviced while the other keeps running.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Package / system",
    "configuration": "Wet-well submersible lift station, duty/standby",
    "application": "Municipal and building wastewater, storm water"
  },
  "model_configuration": {
    "pumps": "2 × submersible non-clog pumps (duty/standby, alternating)",
    "controls": "4 float switches: stop, duty start, standby start, high-level alarm",
    "design_note": "Wet-well volume is sized to limit motor starts per hour (manufacturer limit) and septic retention time."
  },
